From da2f605ef8c877505094f177fa2bb42c94d8eb30 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: arealjim <6187715+arealjim@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 18 Oct 2026 13:34:36 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 12/23] runtime: encoded bytes per frame on the encode queue
 line, oxrsys_encoder_bench

The encode queue log line now ends with frameBytes(min/med/max)=a/b/c small=k/n,
the encoded size of each frame in the window and the count under 20 % of the
median, so duplicate frames reaching the encoder can be counted from the log.
SummarizeEncodedFrameBytes lives in EncodedFrameStats.h with a unit test.

oxrsys_encoder_bench drives the runtime VideoEncoder (real VideoToolbox setup,
Metal compose, video-range conversion) with a GPU-rendered moving pattern and
prints submit-to-callback latency percentiles. Measured 2026-10-18 on the M5 Pro
beside a live 2560x1120 rtvc stream, sparse 15 Hz submission: 2560x1120 callback
p10 9.2 ms with encoder_low_latency on (rtvc), 5.8 ms with it off (ave);
3456x1536 13.7 vs 8.3 ms. Not switched: the October 17 isolated runs measured
the ave session at 12.6 ms (72 Hz, 2272x1264), so the off number may depend on
the live rtvc stream sharing the engine - a live A/B decides it.

